2026-05-26 16:56:03,445 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: **Executive Summary**

Nexus Engineering S.r.l., a consortium of specialized agents, proposes a comprehensive solution to implement an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance tool for the City of Belval's administrative services. Our proposal integrates AI innovation, technical architecture, security compliance, legal eligibility, budget management, and sustainability measures to improve the efficiency and quality of service rendered to users.

**Understanding of Requirements**

We have thoroughly reviewed the call for tenders and understand the City of Belval's objectives, including improving administrative services' efficiency, enhancing user experience, and reducing environmental footprint. Our proposal addresses all aspects of the tender, ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements, such as GDPR, and incorporating measures to minimize energetic consumption and dependence on non-European suppliers.

**Proposed Solution**

Our proposed solution involves designing and deploying a cloud-native AI assistance tool using Large Language Models (LLMs) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities. We will utilize the sovereign model Mistral 7B Instruct, which we have experience with and prefer due to its strong performance on French language tasks, EU origin, and self-hostable nature under the Apache 2.0 license.

For integration with existing systems and business software, we will develop API interfaces using REST and SOAP standards, as well as API gateways like Kong and Apigee. Our expertise in ERP/CRM connectors, including SAP and Oracle, will facilitate seamless interaction between our proposed AI solution and the client's infrastructure.

To ensure security compliance, we will implement several measures, including:

* Hosting all data exclusively within the European Union using Outscale's SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure
* Utilizing anonymization tools, such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, to protect sensitive data
* Implementing encryption methods to protect data both in transit and at rest
* Designing the system to require manual validation by an authorized agent before implementation of AI-driven suggestions or actions

Our budget management approach includes a phased deployment with milestone-based payments, ensuring that costs are optimized while guaranteeing quality. The estimated annual cost of exploitation will be approximately 750,000 EUR, with a projected margin of around 210,000 EUR per year (28% of 750,000 EUR).

To minimize environmental footprint, we will utilize green hosting partners such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, both located in France and using 100% renewable energy. Our digital sobriety practices include INT8/INT4 model quantization, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and implementing a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

**Unaddressed Requirements**

None of the requirements from the tender were left unaddressed in our proposal. We have explicitly stated how we will meet each requirement, using exact technologies, costs, regulations, and figures as stated by our agents.

**Conclusion**

Nexus Engineering S.r.l.'s proposed solution integrates AI innovation, technical architecture, security compliance, legal eligibility, budget management, and sustainability measures to improve the efficiency and quality of service rendered to users. We are confident that our comprehensive approach will meet the City of Belval's objectives while ensuring regulatory compliance and minimizing environmental footprint. Our team is committed to delivering a successful project, and we look forward to the opportunity to collaborate with the City of Belval.

**Appendix**

* Technical Architecture: Cloud-native AI assistance tool using Mistral 7B Instruct LLM and RAG capabilities, integrated with existing systems using API interfaces (REST, SOAP, Kong, Apigee) and ERP/CRM connectors (SAP, Oracle)
* Security Compliance: Hosting on Outscale's SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure, anonymization tools (Microsoft Presidio, custom NER models), encryption methods, manual validation by authorized agents
* Budget Management: Phased deployment with milestone-based payments, estimated annual cost of exploitation approximately 750,000 EUR, projected margin around 210,000 EUR per year (28% of 750,000 EUR)
* Sustainability Measures: Green hosting partners (OVHcloud, Scaleway), digital sobriety practices (INT8/INT4 model quantization, auto-scaling, query result caching, green IT hardware procurement policy)
